Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:43:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Video Pro mode (port of upstream 0012)

Upstream patch 0012-Add-Video-Pro-mode was written against the stock onyx
MiuiCamera dump. Re-derived against the dyper obfuscation dictionary by
matching structure and string literals rather than class names.

Dyper-side mapping of the stock targets:

  stock smali_classes2/.../ProVideoModuleEntry  -> smali_classes2/.../ProVideoModuleEntry (same)
  stock smali_classes2/K1/g                     -> smali/L1/g            (ProVideoModuleDevice)
  stock smali_classes2/c1/a                     -> smali/d1/a
  stock smali_classes2/.../FragmentModeSelector -> same file
  stock smali/b0/x                              -> smali/c0/w            (getTopBarData)
  stock Lo2/a; (ModeItem)                       -> Lp2/a;
  stock drawable 0x7f08055b                     -> 0x7f08055d (ic_mode_pro_cv)
  stock string  0x7f140590 ("Pro video")        -> 0x7f14058d (flc, "Pro video")

  (resource names resolved by dumping the stock APK with aapt2 and re-pinning
   the names against this tree's res/values/public.xml)

Changes:
* ProVideoModuleEntry.support() -> true (was gated on Lv7/b;->B1()Z).
* ProVideoModuleEntry.getModeItem() added so the tab has an icon and label.
* L1/g (ProVideoModuleDevice).D() -> true (was Lcom/android/camera/data/data/k;->B(0xb4)).
* d1/a: drop the "Unsupported Slow Motion Recording" throw, fall through instead.
* FragmentModeSelector: drop the 0xa7 -> 0xb4 remap guarded by
  pref_camera_from_pro_video_module.
* c0/w.getTopBarData: when the per-mode top-bar config is empty and the mode is
  Pro Video (0xb4), return the hardcoded item list
  {0xc1, 0xa0, 0xd8, 0xd8, 0xad, 0xae, 0x104, 0xd6, 0xd2} instead of the empty
  singleton, so the mode is not left without controls.

Two deliberate deviations from upstream:
* getTopBarData keys off the requested mode id (saved into v6 before p1 is
  reused for the list) instead of stock's global current-mode singleton
  LZ/a;->g()Le0/o;->s:I. The dyper equivalent of that field could not be
  mapped with confidence; the requested id is what E(I) is called with, so the
  behaviour is equivalent.
* Upstream also touched smali/e0/p.smali (:cond_1d const/4 v6, 0x1 -> 0x0).
  That hunk is NOT ported - the class has no identifiable counterpart in this
  dump (dyper's e0 package stops at e0/i). Flagged rather than guessed.

Pro Video is registered in smali/b1/a (the module-entry table) in the stock
dyper dump already, so support() was the only thing hiding it.

Signed-off-by: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
